msgstr "Deferring to {name}, presently at {n}%."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "Following {name} once a strip has Follow monitor brightness on."
msgstr "Deferring to {name} once a strip defers to the looking-glass."

msgid ""
"ddcutil isn't installed, so no monitor brightness can be read. Install ddcutil sets it up (it "
"asks for your password), or install the ddcutil package yourself and press Look again."
msgstr ""
"ddcutil is not installed, so no looking-glass brightness may be read. Install ddcutil sees to it "
"(it asks for your password), or kindly install the ddcutil package yourself and have another "
"look."

msgid ""
"ddcutil finds no monitor. Some docks and adapters don't pass brightness through, and after "
"installing Iridia you may need to log out and in once."
msgstr ""
"ddcutil finds no looking-glass. Certain docks and adapters withhold the brightness, and after "
"installing Iridia one may need to log out and in once."

msgid "No monitor answers. Turn DDC/CI on in the monitor's own menu, then press Look again."
msgstr "No looking-glass responds. Kindly enable DDC/CI in its own menu, then have another look."

msgid "This monitor doesn't answer. Turn DDC/CI on in its own menu, or pick another one."
msgstr "This looking-glass does not respond. Kindly enable DDC/CI in its own menu, or choose another."

msgid "No monitor brightness to follow."
msgstr "No looking-glass brightness to defer to."

msgid "Strips that follow it use their Manual brightness meanwhile."
msgstr "Strips that defer to it use their By hand brightness meanwhile."

msgid "Lock and idle"
msgstr "Lock and repose"

msgid ""
"Dim or turn off the LEDs when the screen locks or you're away. Strips can stay lit: see "
"Brightness on each strip."
msgstr ""
"Dim or extinguish the lamps when the screen is locked or one has stepped away. Strips may remain "
"lit: see Brightness on each strip."

