msgid "Every LED has its own chip and color (3 pins: 5V, data, GND). Sold as ARGB, RGBIC or digital."
msgstr ""
"Each lamp possesses its own chip and colour (3 pins: 5V, data, GND). Sold as ARGB, RGBIC or "
"digital."

msgid "Addressable 12V in groups (WS2811, COB)"
msgstr "Addressable 12V in companies (WS2811, COB)"

msgid ""
"One chip drives a group of LEDs, so a group is one pixel. OpenRGB counts pixels, not LEDs; set "
"how many LEDs are in a pixel so the Layout tab draws the real length."
msgstr ""
"One chip governs a company of lamps, so a company is one pixel. OpenRGB counts pixels, not lamps;"
" set how many lamps are in a pixel so the Floor Plan draws the true length."

msgid "One color (plain 12V RGB, 4 pins)"
msgstr "One colour (plain 12V RGB, 4 pins)"

msgid ""
"The whole strip shows one color (12V, R, G, B pins). Patterns, painting and color stops don't "
"apply, so they're hidden."
msgstr ""
"The whole strip wears a single colour (12V, R, G, B pins). Patterns, painting and colour stops do"
" not apply, and are discreetly hidden."

msgid "RGBW addressable (SK6812 RGBW, experimental)"
msgstr "RGBW addressable (SK6812 RGBW, experimental)"

msgid ""
"OpenRGB sends 3 bytes per LED, RGBW strips read 4. Iridia packs the white channel into the data "
"itself, which needs the OpenRGB zone to be a third larger than the strip. Assumes the header "
"sends GRB (like WS2812B); use Color order if colors come out swapped. Count LEDs doesn't work on "
"these strips: set the LED count by hand."
msgstr ""
"OpenRGB sends 3 bytes per lamp; RGBW strips read 4. Iridia packs the white channel into the data "
"itself, which requires the OpenRGB zone to be a third larger than the strip. It presumes the "
"header sends GRB (as for WS2812B); use Colour order should colours arrive exchanged. Counting "
"lamps does not serve these strips: set the count by hand."

